From: Roi Blum <roiblum05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:00:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: keep Agents carrying a label out of a NodePool
 (excludeAgentLabels)

An entry's excludeAgentLabels lists Agent label keys its NodePool never
takes an Agent with. Its agentLabelSelector keeps the InfraEnv's matchLabels
and gains matchExpressions: {key: <label>, operator: DoesNotExist} for each.
An empty or missing list adds nothing.

herzi's collector of used Agents labels every Agent installed in a cluster
and deletes a free one that carries the label; excluding the label keeps a
freed used Agent from being bound again before herzi deletes it.

On an InPlace NodePool (the default) the change touches no running node; on
a Replace NodePool it replaces every node. Without the key the render is
unchanged: the golden parity tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016gPPBP4UxCerc81DKaJHKm
